BT /F2 18.0 Tf 50 779.2 Td (Faculty Entrepreneurship / Technical Start-ups) Tj ET
BT /F2 18.0 Tf 50 741.3 Td (Policy and Procedure \(2026 Revision\)) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.5 Tf 50 714.2 Td (SYNTHETIC EXAMPLE: prepared for the RAHBAR RAGOps evaluation \(Assignment 03, Batch B\). Not an official FAST-NUCES) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.5 Tf 50 701.9 Td (document; nothing in it applies to real students. It imitates the form of a revision of the 2022 policy; its rules) Tj ET
BT /F3 8.5 Tf 50 689.5 Td (are invented.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 676.2 Td (This revision replaces the edition dated 30.05.2022 for applications made after September) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 661.0 Td (2026.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.0 Tf 50 635.0 Td (1. Purpose and scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 615.1 Td (1.1 The policy lets full-time faculty members take part in a technical start-up that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 599.9 Td (commercialises research carried out at the university, and sets out the conditions, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 584.7 Td (application procedure and the reporting duties.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 566.4 Td (1.2 Faculty entrepreneurship means founding or managing a technical start-up, holding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 551.2 Td (significant equity in it, sitting on its governing board or receiving a share of its revenue.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.0 Tf 50 525.2 Td (2. Eligibility) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 505.3 Td (2.1 The applicant must have been a full-time faculty member for more than 2 years.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 487.1 Td (2.2 The start-up must be based on research done at the university. A licensing agreement lets) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 471.9 Td (the start-up use the university's intellectual property at no initial cost for 3 years.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 453.7 Td (2.3 After the no-cost period the license fee is negotiated between the university and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 438.4 Td (start-up.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.0 Tf 50 412.4 Td (3. Evaluation criteria) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 392.6 Td (3.1 The applicant has published at least one journal paper with a DOI, with a university) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 377.3 Td (affiliation, within the three years before the application.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 359.1 Td (3.2 The applicant is, or has been within the last five years, principal or co-principal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 343.9 Td (investigator of an externally funded research project.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.0 Tf 50 317.9 Td (4. Procedure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 298.0 Td (4.1 Applications are submitted through the online portal of the research office \(ORIC\) at any) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 282.8 Td (time of the year, with the prescribed form and a short business plan.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 264.6 Td (4.2 The Campus Director comments and forwards the application to ORIC, which evaluates it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 249.3 Td (within 30 working days and presents it to the Rector. The Rector's decision is final.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.0 Tf 50 223.3 Td (5. Reporting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 203.5 Td (5.1 For the first two years the start-up reports every three months, and every six months) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 188.2 Td (after that: income, jobs created, industry partnerships and patents.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 170.0 Td (5.2 The university may end the license if the reports are not submitted.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13.0 Tf 50 144.0 Td (6. Other conditions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 124.1 Td (6.1 Approval creates no financial or legal liability for the university, and the university) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 108.9 Td (gives no infrastructure or funding for the start-up.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 90.7 Td (6.2 The faculty member may not hold the sole management role. A full-time chief executive or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 50 75.5 Td (managing director runs the company.) Tj ET
